{"note_id":54,"date":"2025-04-02","note_type":"Medical Oncology Consultation","content":"Initial med onc visit 2025-04-02. We reviewed that she has a resected left breast primary with hormone receptor positive, HER2-negative disease and node-negative status after sentinel node sampling. Because the tumor is over 2 cm and the patient is otherwise fit, genomic assay was sent to help estimate benefit of adjuvant chemotherapy. There is no suggestion in the record of a purely in situ process or benign lesion; treatment recommendations are being made for an invasive breast cancer. Staging scans were not ordered because she has no bone pain, cough, weight loss, or abnormal liver tests, and presentation remains consistent with localized disease.","summary":"The patient had a medical oncology consultation to discuss adjuvant management after resection of a hormone‑receptor‑positive, HER2‑negative, node‑negative left‑breast invasive cancer larger than 2 cm. A genomic assay was ordered to estimate the benefit of adjuvant chemotherapy, and no staging scans were performed due to the absence of systemic symptoms.","concepts":{"cancer":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":54,"text":"treatment recommendations are being made for an invasive breast cancer"}]},"metastasis":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"surgery":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":54,"text":"resected left breast primary"}]},"chemotherapy":{"presence":false,"confidence":"medium","evidence":[]},"radiation":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"lymph_nodes_removed":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":54,"text":"node-negative status after sentinel node sampling"}]}},"cancer_status":["current"],"cancer_mentions":[{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":54,"text":"she has a resected left breast primary with hormone receptor positive, HER2-negative disease and node-negative status after sentinel node sampling"}],"status":"current","affected_tissue":"left breast","metastasis":false}],"flags":["medical oncology","breast cancer","adjuvant therapy","genomic assay","staging scans"]}
{"note_id":55,"date":"2025-04-10","note_type":"Systemic Therapy Note","content":"Genomic assay returned in the intermediate-high range, and adjuvant chemotherapy was recommended. Docetaxel/cyclophosphamide cycle 1 was administered on 2025-04-10. She tolerated infusion with expected fatigue and transient metallic taste, no febrile symptoms. Radiation oncology referral placed for adjuvant whole-breast radiation after completion of chemotherapy. Endocrine therapy to follow radiation. The patient asked whether the in situ component changes the main diagnosis; we reviewed that the invasive component drives prognosis and treatment planning.","summary":"An intermediate‑high genomic assay prompted recommendation of adjuvant chemotherapy, and the first docetaxel/cyclophosphamide cycle was administered and tolerated with expected fatigue and metallic taste. A referral for adjuvant whole‑breast radiation after chemotherapy was placed, with endocrine therapy planned thereafter. The patient’s question about the in‑situ component was addressed, emphasizing that the invasive component drives prognosis and treatment planning.","concepts":{"cancer":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":55,"text":"the invasive component drives prognosis and treatment planning"}]},"metastasis":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"surgery":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"chemotherapy":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":55,"text":"Docetaxel/cyclophosphamide cycle 1 was administered on 2025-04-10"}]},"radiation":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":55,"text":"Radiation oncology referral placed for adjuvant whole-breast radiation after completion of chemotherapy"}]},"lymph_nodes_removed":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]}},"cancer_status":["current"],"cancer_mentions":[{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":55,"text":"adjuvant whole-breast radiation after completion of chemotherapy"}],"status":"current","affected_tissue":"breast","metastasis":false}],"flags":["genomic assay","adjuvant chemotherapy","docetaxel/cyclophosphamide","radiation referral","endocrine therapy","invasive component"]}

